# No public hostnames in git

This repository is **public**. Do **not** commit real deployment hostnames, personal domains, or internal URLs.

## Use placeholders instead

- API: `https://kbapp.example.com`, `https://kbapp-staging.example.com`
- Nextcloud: `https://nextcloud.example.com`
- Admin: `https://kbadmin.example.com`
- Allowlists / schema `$id`: `example.com` / `localhost` only

Real URLs belong in **local** `.env`, LaunchAgent plists (not in git), CI **secrets**, or private ops notes — never in README/docs/scripts defaults that ship to GitHub.

## If you find a real hostname in a change

Replace it with a placeholder before commit/push. Do not “document prod” with the live FQDN.
